# Title: Suspicious Service Installed
# ID: f2485272-a156-4773-82d7-1d178bc4905b
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: xknow (@xknow_infosec), xorxes (@xor_xes)
# Date: 2019-04-08
# Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685
# Description: Detects installation of NalDrv or PROCEXP152 services via registry-keys to non-system32 folders.
# Both services are used in the tool Ghost-In-The-Logs (https://github.com/bats3c/Ghost-In-The-Logs), which uses KDU (https://github.com/hfiref0x/KDU)
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((TargetObject:"HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\NalDrv\\ImagePath" OR TargetObject:"HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\PROCEXP152\\ImagePath")) AND -(((process_name:*\\procexp64.exe OR process_name:*\\procexp64a.exe OR process_name:*\\procexp.exe OR process_name:*\\procmon64.exe OR process_name:*\\procmon64a.exe OR process_name:*\\procmon.exe OR process_name:*\\handle.exe OR process_name:*\\handle64.exe OR process_name:*\\handle64a.exe) AND Details:*\\WINDOWS\\system32\\Drivers\\PROCEXP152.SYS*)))
